# Copy this file to .leak-patterns (gitignored, never committed) and fill it in with
# extended-regex patterns matching real identifiers from your own private hub — GA4
# property IDs, client domains, personal domains, OAuth project numbers, anything that
# should never show up in docs/ or scripts/ once you publish or share this checkout.
#
# One extended-regex pattern per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# When tests/test_docs.sh runs and .leak-patterns is absent, the anti-leak check is
# skipped (visibly) rather than silently passing — this file only matters if you create
# a real .leak-patterns locally.
#
# Example patterns (placeholders only — replace with your own real identifiers):
123456789
example-client\.com
example-personal-domain\.com
987654321098
